  "description": "The Human Protein Atlas provides a map showing the distribution and relative abundance of proteins in the human body. All IHC staining in the Human Protein Atlas project are performed using the following standard protocol. The primary antibody dilution is based on titration optimization, the dilution suggested by the Human Protein Atlas can be found under antibody and antigen information for each antibody. When primary antibody originates from other host animals than rabbit, there are some modifications and different secondary antibody is used.                \n",
